@startuml sequence-2-arrival
!include style.iuml
title Restaurant Rush | Turn 7: activate, arrive and seat (sequence 2 of 4)
caption Expands beginTurn(true) and the Host action in the winning branch of page 1.
boundary "ui : ConsoleUI" as UI
control "controller : TurnController" as TC
entity "state : GameState" as State
participant "arrivals : IntFunction<Customer>\n(lambda wired by GameSetup)" as Factory
participant "c3 : RegularCustomer" as C3
participant "host : Host" as Host
participant "Seating\n(package-private static)" as Seating
entity "t1 : Table" as T1
autonumber

note over TC, T1
  Entry: turn 6 completed; C1 PAID, C2 READY_TO_PAY.
  T1 is free; T2 still contains C2 (payment happens later in turn 7).
  UI has parsed HAPPY_HOUR. Failed phase/reuse checks throw before mutation.
end note
UI -> TC : beginTurn(true)
TC -> TC : requirePhase("beginTurn", TURN_START)
TC -> State : happyHourUsed()
State --> TC : false
TC -> State : setTurn(7)
TC -> State : activateHappyHour()
note right of State : Records happyHourTurn = 7; event "Happy Hour activated".
TC -> State : happyHourActive()
State --> TC : true (remaining 2)
TC -> TC : recoverWaitingCustomers(events)
note right of TC
  Iterates existing customers in arrival order:
  C1.recover(15) and C2.recover(15) leave PAID/READY_TO_PAY unchanged.
  C3 does not exist yet. No recovery event at turn 7.
end note
TC -> Factory : apply(3)
note right of Factory
  Lambda calls GameSetup.arrival(3, 7), which constructs
  new RegularCustomer("C3", 7, 3) through the composition root.
end note
Factory --> TC : c3 (WAITING, satisfaction 100)
TC -> State : addCustomer(c3)
TC -> State : queue().add(c3)
note right of State : Arrival event: "C3 (Regular) arrives".
TC -> State : setPhase(HOST)
TC -> TC : snapshot()
TC --> UI : TurnStart(events, snapshot); remaining 2
UI -> TC : submit(Action(HOST, SEAT, "C3"))
TC -> Host : seat(state, "C3")
Host -> Seating : seat(state, "C3")
Seating -> State : queue().find("C3")
State --> Seating : present
Seating -> Seating : firstFreeTable(state)
note right of Seating : Finds T1 from state.tables(), in creation order.
Seating -> State : queue().remove("C3")
State --> Seating : c3
Seating -> T1 : seat("C3")
Seating -> C3 : seat()
note right of C3 : WAITING -> SEATED; satisfaction still 100.
Seating --> Host : accepted; "C3 seated at T1"
Host --> TC : ActionResult
TC -> State : setPhase(WAITER)
TC --> UI : accepted ActionResult
ref over UI, TC : Page 3 continues in the same turn: ORDER C3, then PREPARE O3.

note over State, T1
  Queue and tables are separate: a queued customer can be selected by ID.
  If the ID is not queued or no table is free, Seating returns rejected
  before removal/seating; submit leaves HOST unchanged so UI retries.
  Host uses the same Seating implementation as Waiter.
end note
footer Exact method responsibility matters: Controller calls the arrival factory; Host delegates table selection to Seating.
@enduml
